  "description": "Beasley's capacitated warehouse location problems, test problem sets IV to XIII and A to C, which essentially include the Akinc and Khumawala test problems: 16 to 100 potential warehouses and 50 to 1,000 customers, each customer's whole demand assignable to any warehouse at a stated cost. Each of capa, capb and capc writes the word capacity in place of every warehouse's capacity and stands for four problems, one for each capacity Table 1 of Beasley (1988) gives, so the 37 files are 49 problems.",
